(a) Both subclasses **inherit** the attribute `name` and the constructor part of `Person`. `Student` adds `form`, `Teacher` adds `subject`, and both **override** `describe()`, each calling the version of `Person` and adding its own text.

```
class Person:
    def __init__(self, name):
        self.name = name
    def describe(self):
        return self.name

class Student(Person):
    def __init__(self, name, form):
        Person.__init__(self, name)
        self.form = form
    def describe(self):
        return Person.describe(self) + " - " + self.form

class Teacher(Person):
    def __init__(self, name, subject):
        Person.__init__(self, name)
        self.subject = subject
    def describe(self):
        return Person.describe(self) + " teaches " + self.subject
```

