(c) The loop only sends the message `describe()` to each object. Because of **polymorphism**, a new subclass `Bursar` that overrides `describe()` works with the same loop without any change, and the code of `Person` is reused through **inheritance**. This is why object-oriented programs are easy to extend. The code is an example of the logic and was run to check the three lines.
